  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TA Support to PAVM Secretariat/Africa CDC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The objective of this support will be to enhance the agenda setting and coordination role of the AU/Africa CDC in the operationalization of the PAVM Framework for Action.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;Specific objective(s):&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;o&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;The first specific objective will be to deploy one technical expert in the PAVM Secretariat to work on one or more of the PAVM work streams to be jointly decided with Africa CDC.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;o&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;The expert will help prepare further EC support.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Partnerships for African Vaccine Manufacturing (PAVM) was established by the African Union (AU) in 2021 to deliver a bold goal: enabling the African vaccine manufacturing industry to develop, produce, and supply over 60 percent of the total vaccine doses required on the continent by 2040, up from less than 1 percent today (with interim goals of 10 percent by 2025 and 30 percent by 2030).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;Implementing this strategy will require several parallel programs and supporting initiatives and pilots. These include the consolidation and oversight of ongoing vaccine manufacturing projects, the creation and maintenance of investment relationships, the streamlining of existing and proposed capability and capacity centres, and advocacy for supportive policies across the ecosystem. PAVM has been designed by African entities for African manufacturers as an integral part of the Agenda 2063. PAVM is composed of a Task Force that, along with the Secretariat, oversees, steers, and supervises seven work streams.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;The PAVM Secretariat will play the crucial role of managing the day to day activities related to the coordination and implementation of the PAVM Framework for Action. In particular, facilitating the agenda setting and coordination role of the AU/Africa CDC.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
